text:
ashley: opened a small docs PR to make function/tool outputs tolerant: shift from top-level "output" to a nullable "result" envelope. PR: https://git.redwood/infer/docs/pull/909

mike: short example?

ashley: before: {"tool":"lookup", "output": {"id": 1}}
after: {"tool":"lookup", "result": {"payload": {"id": 1}, "confidence": 0.9}}
or: {"tool":"lookup", "result": null}

priya: SDK plan: add parseRelaxed() to TS SDK. Try strict JSON, then small sanitizer (trim trailing commas, fix unquoted keys), fallback to JSON5. Add unit tests for trailing commas, bare tokens, and null envelopes.

jordan: i'll grep examples and patch obvious literal examples; ambiguous cases get // REVIEW comment. will open examples PR with conservative changes.

doc_bot: docs CI: build queued. Current run shows a few snapshot diffs referencing "output". https://ci.redwood/infer/1310

mike: once jordan's examples PR lands i will run smoke locally and in CI. please tag me.

ashley: timeline: land schema + SDK helpers today; examples follow. i'll add a short migration blurb in Structured Outputs explaining nullable "result" and optional "reason" field. tag me for reviews. :thumbsup:
